{"name":"Indiscreet","hex":"#ac3b3b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"indiscreet","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Not discreet; lacking in discretion."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/indiscreet"}],"entries":[{"title":"Indiscreet (1931 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Indiscreet is a 1931 American pre-Code comedy film directed by Leo McCarey and starring Gloria Swanson and Ben Lyon. The screenplay by Buddy G. DeSylva, Lew Brown, and Ray Henderson, based on their story Obey That Impulse, originally was written as a full-fledged musical, but only two songs – \"If You Haven't Got Love\" and \"Come to Me\" – remained when the film was released. The film is available on DVD."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c6/Indiscreet-1931.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indiscreet_(1931_film)","wikidata":"Q3150490"},{"title":"Indiscreet (1958 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Indiscreet is a 1958 British romantic comedy film produced and directed by Stanley Donen, and starring Ingrid Bergman and Cary Grant."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/a6/Indiscreet75.jpg/330px-Indiscreet75.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indiscreet_(1958_film)","wikidata":"Q1462145"},{"title":"Indiscreet (Sparks album)","blocks":[{"text":"Indiscreet is the fifth studio album by Sparks, released in October 1975 by Island Records. While retaining the glam rock sound of Kimono My House and Propaganda, the album emphasised the theatrical elements of their work, with greater use of orchestral arrangements and drawing from non-rock orientated styles such as jazz, big band, swing, vaudeville, and classical music. The album was produced by Tony Visconti, with whom the group reunited in 1997 to produce several tracks for their retrospective album Plagiarism. The song \"How Are You Getting Home?\" was used in Leos Carax's film Holy Motors."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/2a/Indiscreet_-_Sparks.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indiscreet_(Sparks_album)","wikidata":"Q6025149"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Grant_Bergman_Indiscreet_Still.jpg/500px-Grant_Bergman_Indiscreet_Still.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Grant_Bergman_Indiscreet_Still.jpg/1280px-Grant_Bergman_Indiscreet_Still.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Grant_Bergman_Indiscreet_Still.jpg/500px-Grant_Bergman_Indiscreet_Still.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cary Grant and Ingrid Bergman in the romantic comedy film Indiscreet.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGrant_Bergman_Indiscreet_Still.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Cary_Grant_%26_Ingrid_Bergman_Indiscreet_still.jpg/500px-Cary_Grant_%26_Ingrid_Bergman_Indiscreet_still.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Cary_Grant_%26_Ingrid_Bergman_Indiscreet_still.jpg/500px-Cary_Grant_%26_Ingrid_Bergman_Indiscreet_still.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cary Grant as Philip Adams and Ingrid Bergman as Anna Kalman.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACary_Grant_%26_Ingrid_Bergman_Indiscreet_still.jpg"}],"sounds":{"indiscreet":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/ab/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-indiscreet.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=o